{
  "requirement": "The `Markdown` implementation of `OutlineLang` supplies the extension, selection, and fingerprint rules described in this chapter.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub struct Markdown;\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Clone for Markdown;\nimpl Debug for Markdown;\nimpl Default for Markdown;\nimpl OutlineLang for Markdown;\nimpl Copy for Markdown;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject declares the `Markdown` unit struct and its trait implementations. It delegates the extension, selection and fingerprint rules to the chapter's refining requirements: `requirements.sdk.sources.markdown.language`, `.sections`, `.fingerprints` and the others. Those are assessed under their own requirements, not here.\n\nObligations assessed here, and the tests that cover them:\n- **`OutlineLang` implementation:** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs#fn[bundled_languages_claim_extensions_and_supply_the_same_public_outline]` calls its inner `check` helper with `languages::Markdown`. The helper asserts `name()` is non-empty, `extensions()` equals `[\"md\",\"markdown\"]`, and `fingerprint_scheme()` equals `markdown-structural-v1`. It also checks that the file name `a.MARKDOWN` infers the language and produces `section[Check]`. `fn[markdown_heading_levels_resolve_encoded_duplicates_and_anonymous_items]` further exercises Markdown outline items, selection and spans through `OutlineContent`.\n- **`Clone`, `Copy` and `Default`:** The `check` helper is bounded `L: OutlineLang + Default + Copy`, so the test only compiles if `Markdown` implements `Copy` and `Default`. It calls `Clone::clone` and asserts the clone reports the same extensions. It asserts `L::default().fingerprint_scheme()` equals the expected scheme. It also asserts the struct is zero-sized, which matches `pub struct Markdown;`.\n- **Public shape:** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` checks the `Markdown` struct's path and kind against rustdoc and the appendix.\n\n`Debug` has no direct test. It is a derived implementation with no conditional logic, and the text specifies no output format. No requirement-violating behavior could slip through, so I did not count this as a gap.\n\nI found no unacknowledged gaps and no marking gaps. Both Markdown tests carry `{test}` references to the subject.",
